        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_35.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dyrne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dyrne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_35.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_35.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-gyld <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-gyld Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Statt Instr. setzt B moderner Präposition</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In place of the instrumental B puts a more modern preposition</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o.</hi> 16. 21; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Beweisnähe 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 16. 21; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Beweisnähe 6</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Widerstand der Dieb der Fesselung nicht, so durfte er ihn also, folgert Laughlin <hi rend="italic">Essays in Ags. law</hi> 275, nicht töten. Dies steht nicht hier und widerspricht anderen Stellen; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Diebstahl 11a. b; handhaft 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">If the thief did not resist being bound, then, Laughlin <hi rend="italic">Essays in Ags. law</hi> 275 concludes, the man might not kill him. This is not stated here and contradicts other passages; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Diebstahl 11a. b; handhaft 11</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q missversteht, der Totschläger schwöre der Sippe des Erschlagenen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q misunderstands it to mean that the slayer swears to the kindred of the slain man</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Über <hi rend="italic">ceas(t) s.</hi> Af El 18¹. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Urfehde. Q, an <hi rend="italic">ceosan</hi> ‘küren’ denkend, missversteht den <hi rend="italic">ungecoren að,</hi> das Gegenteil vom ‘Auswahleid’; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On <hi rend="italic">ceas(t) see</hi> Af El 18¹. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Urfehde. Q, thinking of <hi rend="italic">ceosan</hi> ‘choose’, misunderstands the <hi rend="italic">ungecoren að,</hi> the opposite of the ‘selected oath’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_35.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">74</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hinzuzudenken ist, dass des Erschlagenen Sippe Wergeld für den Erschlagenen eingeklagt hat, dem Beweise näher, da Kundmachung (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 1) durch Täter verabsäumt war</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">It is to be understood that the slain man’s kindred has sued for wergild for him, and is nearer to proof, since the slayer had failed to make a declaration (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 1)</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_35.attnote.fn.17" n="17" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>aðe</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mid aðe</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_35.attnote.fn.18" n="18" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>fleondne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">fleonde</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_35.attnote.fn.19" n="19" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>unceases</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">unceastes</hi>. H.</seg></note>
      </div>
